-## Unchanged limitations
-
-- The separate `same_support` heuristic and distance-based original-edge
-  selection remain unchanged. Exact face identity does not eliminate these
-  geometric searches or correct their existing limitations.
-- The existing `occt_precision`, `occt_maxprecision`, `sameparameter`, and
-  `surfacecurve_mode` options remain parsed/reported but have no effect on the
-  old reader routines. Activating them would change the numerical baseline.
-- The edge-length filter retains the old six-decimal `std::to_string` conversion
-  of `cad_edge_tol_fraction` before OCC calculations.
-- Existing numerical fallbacks, projection counters, sampled continuity
-  helpers and solver tolerances remain unchanged. Successful construction is
-  not a certificate of polynomial-to-CAD accuracy or watertightness.
-- The original Gmsh session lifecycle clears models. Do not share a Gmsh model
-  with a mesher invocation; mesher calls are serialized within the native core.
-- CAD area and refinement self-convergence remain the original diagnostics;
-  neither makes the old mesh an independent exact geometry reference.
-
-The migration report in `docs/V3_NATIVE_IDENTITY_MIGRATION.md` records baseline
-provenance, numerical comparisons, test results, and any incomplete gates.
+This extraction does not add V2 repairs, automatic refinement, automatic order
+selection, or new numerical tolerances. The existing `same_support` heuristic,
+original-edge searches, inactive reader options, and six-decimal edge-tolerance
+conversion are retained. Successful construction, area agreement, and
+self-convergence do not certify polynomial-to-CAD accuracy or watertightness.
+The original torus's irregular coarse-mesh convergence remains a known
+limitation; its regression tests are not an absolute accuracy guarantee.
